Round 5 (2026-02-26)

What changed this round
- Final code change: `clang/aot/emit.c` only.
- Added inline DUP forcing in compiled strict `OP2` paths:
  - after emitting lhs (`arg+0`), if lhs is `DP0/DP1`, emit `lhs = aot_force_dup(lhs)`;
  - in the `lhs == NUM` branch, after emitting rhs (`arg+1`), if rhs is `DP0/DP1`, emit `rhs = aot_force_dup(rhs)`.
- This follows expert guidance A1: when strict local WNF touches env-bound DP vars, try inline DUP interactions first instead of dropping to interpreter behavior.

Attempted but reverted (important)
- I implemented a broader strict helper in `clang/aot/_.c` (`aot_force_strict`) that forced `DP` + opened `ALO` and wired it into head `SWI/MAT/OP2`.
- This was UNSAFE: AOT tests regressed immediately (`collapse_supgen_mul`, `enum_primes`, `factorial`, `fib*`), including segfaults and `cannot apply a number` runtime errors.
- Root lesson: naively opening ALO at strict sites breaks invariants; broad strict forcing should not be reintroduced without a much tighter correctness model.
- Reverted all of that, restored previous `SWI/MAT` behavior, kept only OP2 DP forcing.

